# Rule Triggers

When any condition below applies, fetch the named rule before proceeding.

| Condition | Fetch rule |
|-----------|------------|
| Working with an external library or API | @context7-usage |
| Breaking change / major version bump | @breaking-change-major-version-protocol |
| Creating, moving, or refactoring a schema type | @schema-governance-index |
| Working with provider API schemas or `__api_version__` | @provider-api-version-manifest |
| Defining semver version constants in UAC/UIC schema files | @canonical-schema-semver |
| Creating or placing a plan file | @plan-placement |
| Rolling out a change across multiple repos | @rollout-tracking |
| Spawning or coordinating sub-agents | @sub-agent-workflow-standard |
| Running independent tasks across multiple repos | @parallel-agent-execution |
| About to implement something from scratch | @search-before-implementing |
| Context window is large / optimizing token usage | @token-optimization |
| Doing codebase architecture analysis | @accurate-codebase-analysis |
| Following a plan through to deployable code | @plans-to-deployable-workflow |
| Creating or setting up a new repo | @mandatory-setup-sh |
| Configuring git hooks | @hook-tooling-policy |
| Running or debugging quality gates | @strict-quality-gates |
| Reviewing common anti-patterns | @anti-patterns-quick-reference |
